   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "תַּנְיָא, הָיָה רַבִּי מֵאִיר אוֹמֵר: כׇּל הַמַּשִּׂיא בִּתּוֹ לְעַם הָאָרֶץ, כְּאִילּוּ כּוֹפְתָהּ וּמַנִּיחָהּ לִפְנֵי אֲרִי. מָה אֲרִי דּוֹרֵס וְאוֹכֵל, וְאֵין לוֹ בּוֹשֶׁת פָּנִים — אַף עַם הָאָרֶץ מַכֶּה וּבוֹעֵל, וְאֵין לוֹ בּוֹשֶׁת פָּנִים.",
   "en": "«It was taught» in a baraita that «Rabbi Meir would say: Anyone who marries off his daughter to an ignoramus» is considered «as though he binds her and places her before a lion.» Why is this so? «Just as a lion mauls» its prey «and eats and has no shame, so too, an ignoramus strikes» his wife «and» then «engages in sexual relations» with her without appeasing her first, «and has no shame.»"
  }
